{
  "format": "srwb",
  "version": "1.0",
  "notebook": {
    "name": "Prolog Generates Lua: Compiler Demo",
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "# Prolog Generates Lua\n\nThis workbook demonstrates UnifyWeaver compiling Prolog predicates into **Lua** code.\n\nTwo input modes are shown:\n1. **Embedded** — facts compiled directly into the Lua code\n2. **VFS** — facts read from another notebook cell at runtime\n\n**Requires:** Install the UnifyWeaver package first (Browse Packages).",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Load UnifyWeaver compiler modules\n['../init'].\n:- use_module(unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "load_compiler"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Define a family tree as Prolog facts\n:- dynamic parent/2, ancestor/2.\n\nparent(alice, bob).\nparent(bob, charlie).\nparent(bob, diana).\nparent(charlie, eve).\nparent(diana, frank).\n\n% Transitive closure: ancestor(X, Y) if X is an ancestor of Y\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Y).\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Z), ancestor(Z, Y).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "family_tree"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "## Pattern 1: Embedded Input\n\nUsing `input(embedded)`, the Prolog facts are compiled directly into the Lua code as `add_fact()` calls. The generated code is self-contained — no external data needed.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Compile with input(embedded) — facts baked into the code\nrecursive_compiler:compile_recursive(ancestor/2, [target(lua), input(embedded)], Code),\nformat(string(Queries), '~n~n-- Queries~nlocal results = find_all(\"alice\")~nprint(\"Descendants of alice: \" .. table.concat(results, \", \"))~nprint(\"alice -> eve: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"eve\")))~nprint(\"alice -> frank: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"frank\")))~n', []),\nformat(string(FullCode), '~w~w', [Code, Queries]),\nuser:nb_write('lua_embedded', '.code', FullCode),\nwriteln('Lua code (embedded) written to cell: lua_embedded').",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "compile_embedded"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "-- This cell will be populated by the compiler.\n-- Run the 'compile_embedded' cell above first.",
        "language": "lua",
        "name": "lua_embedded"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "## Pattern 2: VFS Input\n\nUsing `input(vfs(facts_data))`, the generated Lua reads facts from another cell at runtime via the NotebookVFS. This allows the data to be changed without recompiling.\n\nFirst, create a data cell with facts in `from:to` format:",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "alice:bob\nbob:charlie\nbob:diana\ncharlie:eve\ndiana:frank",
        "language": "lua",
        "name": "facts_data"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Compile with input(vfs(facts_data)) — reads from the cell above\nrecursive_compiler:compile_recursive(ancestor/2, [target(lua), input(vfs(facts_data))], Code),\nformat(string(Queries), '~n~n-- Queries~nlocal results = find_all(\"alice\")~nprint(\"Descendants of alice: \" .. table.concat(results, \", \"))~nprint(\"alice -> eve: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"eve\")))~nprint(\"alice -> frank: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"frank\")))~n', []),\nformat(string(FullCode), '~w~w', [Code, Queries]),\nuser:nb_write('lua_vfs', '.code', FullCode),\nwriteln('Lua code (VFS) written to cell: lua_vfs').",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "compile_vfs"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "-- This cell will be populated by the compiler.\n-- Run the 'compile_vfs' cell above first.",
        "language": "lua",
        "name": "lua_vfs"
      }
    ]
  }
}
